TEXT -440 48 Left 4 ;At the variable autotransformer one part of the energy\nis magnetically transferred another part is direct \ntransferred (galvanic) by the autotransformer.\nIf you alternatively set Uvar to 480V the magnetizing \ncurrent is zero and the whole current is galvanically \ntransferred  from the primary side as you will \nsee at picture2\nThe short circuit current of the autotransformer \nis much higher especially if U1 and U2 are of nearly \nthe same height.\nNOTE: The short circuit voltage uk=sqrt(ur*ur+ux*ux)\nis only valid for the middle position of the tap \n(240V). For other tap positions the value varies
